sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-argonauta-argo-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-argonauta-argo-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-argonauta-argo-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Argonauta argo Schnakenberg critical mode at the 95 µm Holocene tier — MorphoEval overall 86.5/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2 keeps the Schnakenberg critical mode (r=0.99934, halo 85.87 µm versus the 95 µm tier, λ=170.03 µm, σ(k_c)=0.200, ablation σ_max=-0.100) and selects procedural grain amplitude 0.40. Computer-vision similarity of the 12-frame 800×600 growth GIF rises from 80.2 (smooth control) to 86.2. Grained-field coherency is 0.290 against the plate's 0.203 (the smooth field was 0.998). γ sweep is monotone, 229.3 µm to 109.8 µm. Overall 86.5/100. Second assessor, nanopub signing, and n=1 remain open. Overall 86.5/100 (faithfulness 86.1, reproducibility 87.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0e502ec97af571f7d94f76469868477feaaf61eb; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 87, Morphological realism / specimen match 84, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 87, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 85, Reproducibility package 87. Output judged: docs/media/argonauta_argo_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-argonauta-argo-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0e502ec97af571f7d94f76469868477feaaf61eb, image/gif, 2920167 B, 800×600 px, 12 frames, artifact_sha256 f5425cac4f1ddbd57ef5661cc24cb1dc4e785975f44522d4274de5260c3556df (sha256 f5425cac4f1ddbd57ef5661cc24cb1dc4e785975f44522d4274de5260c3556df), spec_fingerprint 54b806e24537aefcedcf7233858405c3246c56ac09b2d0e212f862aff5e91fe3. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 54b806e24537aefcedcf7233858405c3246c56ac09b2d0e212f862aff5e91fe3; artifact_sha256: f5425cac4f1ddbd57ef5661cc24cb1dc4e785975f44522d4274de5260c3556df; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/argonauta_argo_turing_wavelength_s0/argonauta_argo_shell_cc0.jpg=b3b1284cdbe9512b..., datasets/argonauta_argo_turing_wavelength_s0/argonauta_argo_turing_wavelength_s0_specimen.jpg=4d2cfc3367b264b3..., datasets/argonauta_argo_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=97c63e114209a765...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-argonauta-argo-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952) selects a finite critical wavenumber when the inhibitor out-diffuses the activator and the reaction Jacobian is stable without diffusion. | Gierer & Meinhardt (1972) and Murray (1981) place spots and ocelli in that class. | Finn & Norman (2010) describe the female Argonauta argo brood shell as a buoyancy organ.; reconstructed_in_script: Critical radial mode fitted to the 100 µm plate, length unit set so analytical λ_c equals the measured 170.03 µm period. | Procedural Gaussian grain (seed 3121), amplitude chosen by a sweep of CV similarity. Phases are not copied from the plate. | Equal-diffusion ablation and a γ sweep.; transfer_boundary: The CC0 whole-shell photograph is a scale control (rib autocorrelation fraction 0.088 versus ocellus period fraction 0.234), not a 95 µm measurement. It has no scale bar.; does_not_claim: Finn & Norman did not measure a 95 µm wavelength. | The gallery plate is a prepared species-gallery image, not a Finn figure and not a population sample. | D_u and D_v are not measured diffusivities. | No predecessor chronospecies is claimed. The series is Holocene 1/1 at 0 Ma.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: R1 resolved: grain sweep selects amplitude 0.40 and lifts GIF CV from 80.2 to 86.2.",
            "remediation needed: R2 resolved: coherency is measured on the grained frame (0.290) against the plate (0.203), not on the smooth field (0.998).",
            "remediation needed: R3 open: no independent second assessor.",
            "remediation needed: R4 open: nanopub profile absent; signatures were not fabricated.",
            "remediation needed: R5 open: n=1 gallery plate." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.865"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single-agent round; second assessor not run)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

